FLAW IN THE ORIGINAL zeta_stationarity.py
  model_information_current(sigma, t) ignores t and peaks at σ=1/2 by hand.
  Midpoints and random t therefore get the same YES verdict as zeta zeros.
  This script uses construction A (Dual-Zero spectral zeta of the conoid Dirac
  operator) and does not insert zeros into J.

Gradient of S_I at σ=1/2 (smaller would mean 'more stationary'):
  zeros:      n=79  median |∇S_I|=7.746  mean=7.747
  midpoints:  n=79  median |∇S_I|=7.746  mean=7.747
  random t:   n=79  median |∇S_I|=7.748  mean=7.749

